---
import Layout from '@/components/astro/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About — Breakpoint">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
    <a href="/" class="text-sm text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-900 dark:hover:text-neutral-100">← Home</a>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-6">About Breakpoint</h1>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Most learning platforms teach you to <em>build</em>. Breakpoint teaches you to <em>diagnose</em> —
        because that's where junior engineers actually struggle on the job.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each challenge is a small project with a real bug. You don't get told the answer. You read,
        predict, run, observe, hypothesize. When you patch it, a concept card explains the mental model
        the bug exposed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Open source under MIT.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
